# Accessibility and UI Rules

## Color Contrast and Text Visibility

### Critical Rule: Text and Background Color Contrast

**NEVER use the same or similar colors for text and background** - this makes content invisible or unreadable.

#### ❌ BAD Examples - Invisible or Low Contrast Text

```tsx
// Same color - text is invisible
<div className="bg-gray-100 text-gray-100">
  Invisible text
</div>

// Very low contrast - hard to read
<div className="bg-gray-200 text-gray-300">
  Low contrast text
</div>

// White on light background
<div className="bg-gray-50 text-white">
  Poor visibility
</div>

// Dark text on dark background
<div className="bg-gray-900 text-gray-800">
  Invisible text
</div>
```

#### ✅ GOOD Examples - High Contrast Text

```tsx
// Dark text on light background
<div className="bg-white text-gray-900">
  High contrast text
</div>

<div className="bg-gray-50 text-gray-900">
  Good visibility
</div>

// Light text on dark background
<div className="bg-gray-900 text-white">
  High contrast text
</div>

<div className="bg-blue-600 text-white">
  Good visibility
</div>

// Medium backgrounds need appropriate text color
<div className="bg-gray-500 text-white">
  Light text on medium background
</div>

<div className="bg-gray-400 text-gray-900">
  Dark text on medium background
</div>
```

### Contrast Ratio Guidelines (WCAG)

Follow Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) for contrast ratios:

- **Normal text (< 18pt)**: Minimum contrast ratio of **4.5:1** (Level AA)
- **Large text (≥ 18pt or 14pt bold)**: Minimum contrast ratio of **3:1** (Level AA)
- **Enhanced (Level AAA)**: 
  - Normal text: **7:1**
  - Large text: **4.5:1**

### Tailwind Color Combinations

#### Light Backgrounds (50-300)
Use **dark text** (600-900):
```tsx
<div className="bg-gray-50 text-gray-900">   // ✅ Good
<div className="bg-blue-100 text-blue-900">  // ✅ Good
<div className="bg-red-100 text-red-800">    // ✅ Good
```

#### Medium Backgrounds (400-600)
Use **white or very dark text**:
```tsx
<div className="bg-gray-500 text-white">     // ✅ Good
<div className="bg-blue-600 text-white">     // ✅ Good
<div className="bg-red-500 text-white">      // ✅ Good
```

#### Dark Backgrounds (700-900)
Use **white or very light text** (50-100):
```tsx
<div className="bg-gray-900 text-white">     // ✅ Good
<div className="bg-blue-800 text-blue-50">   // ✅ Good
<div className="bg-red-900 text-red-100">    // ✅ Good
```

### Common Patterns in This Project

#### Buttons
```tsx
// Primary button - dark background, white text
<button className="bg-blue-600 text-white hover:bg-blue-700">
  Primary Action
</button>

// Secondary button - light background, dark text
<button className="bg-gray-100 text-gray-900 hover:bg-gray-200">
  Secondary Action
</button>

// Danger button - red background, white text
<button className="bg-red-600 text-white hover:bg-red-700">
  Delete
</button>
```

#### Cards
```tsx
// White card with dark text
<div className="bg-white rounded-lg shadow p-4">
  <h3 className="text-gray-900 font-bold">Title</h3>
  <p className="text-gray-600">Description text</p>
</div>

// Colored card with appropriate text
<div className="bg-blue-600 rounded-lg shadow p-4">
  <h3 className="text-white font-bold">Title</h3>
  <p className="text-blue-100">Description text</p>
</div>
```

#### Status Indicators
```tsx
// Success - green background, appropriate text
<div className="bg-green-100 text-green-800 border border-green-300 rounded px-2 py-1">
  Success
</div>

// Warning - yellow background, dark text
<div className="bg-yellow-50 text-yellow-800 border border-yellow-300 rounded px-2 py-1">
  Warning
</div>

// Error - red background, dark or white text
<div className="bg-red-100 text-red-800 border border-red-300 rounded px-2 py-1">
  Error
</div>

// Info - blue background, appropriate text
<div className="bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 border border-blue-300 rounded px-2 py-1">
  Info
</div>
```

### Text Variants

#### Primary Text
Use the darkest color on light backgrounds:
```tsx
<p className="text-gray-900">Primary text content</p>
```

#### Secondary Text
Use medium-dark colors for less emphasis:
```tsx
<p className="text-gray-600">Secondary descriptive text</p>
```

#### Muted Text
Use lighter colors but maintain readability:
```tsx
<p className="text-gray-500">Muted helper text</p>
```

#### Disabled Text
Use lighter colors to indicate disabled state:
```tsx
<p className="text-gray-400">Disabled text</p>
```

### Form Inputs

Always specify text color and background explicitly for form inputs:

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - Explicit text color and background
<input
  type="text"
  className="w-full px-3 py-2 text-gray-900 bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-lg 
             focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:border-blue-500
             placeholder:text-gray-400"
  placeholder="Enter value"
/>

<input
  type="date"
  className="w-full px-3 py-2 text-gray-900 bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-lg 
             focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:border-blue-500"
/>

<textarea
  className="w-full px-3 py-2 text-gray-900 bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-lg 
             focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:border-blue-500
             placeholder:text-gray-400"
  placeholder="Enter description"
/>

// ❌ BAD - Missing text color (browser default may vary)
<input
  type="text"
  className="w-full px-3 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg"
/>

// Labels should also have good contrast
<label className="block text-xs font-medium text-gray-700 mb-1">
  Field Label
</label>

// Disabled/readonly inputs
<input
  type="date"
  value="2025-01-15"
  readOnly
  disabled
  className="w-full px-3 py-2 text-gray-700 bg-gray-100 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg 
             cursor-not-allowed"
/>
```

**Key Points for Form Inputs:**
- ✅ Always use `text-gray-900` for active input text
- ✅ Always use `bg-white` for active input background
- ✅ Use `text-gray-700 bg-gray-100` for disabled/readonly inputs
- ✅ Add `cursor-not-allowed` to disabled inputs for better UX
- ✅ Set `max` attribute on date inputs to prevent future dates when needed
- ✅ For date range filters: end date should be today (readonly), start date is user-editable
- ✅ Auto-apply date changes (no manual "Apply" button needed) for better UX

### Interactive States

Ensure hover, focus, and active states also maintain contrast:

```tsx
<button className="
  bg-blue-600 text-white 
  hover:bg-blue-700 hover:text-white
  focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:ring-offset-2
  disabled:bg-gray-300 disabled:text-gray-500
">
  Interactive Button
</button>
```

### Gradient Backgrounds

When using gradients, ensure text remains readable across the entire gradient:

```tsx
// ✅ Good - white text visible on entire gradient
<div className="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-600 to-blue-700 text-white">
  Readable across gradient
</div>

// ❌ Bad - text might be invisible on parts of gradient
<div className="bg-gradient-to-r from-white to-gray-900 text-gray-500">
  Invisible on white part
</div>
```

### Testing Contrast

Before committing code with new color combinations:

1. **Visual Check**: Can you easily read the text?
2. **Squint Test**: If you squint, can you still see the text?
3. **Grayscale Test**: Does it work in grayscale?
4. **Use Browser DevTools**: Check contrast ratio in accessibility panel
5. **Online Tools**: Use WebAIM Contrast Checker (https://webaim.org/resources/contrastchecker/)

### Common Mistakes to Avoid

```tsx
// ❌ NEVER DO THIS
<div className="bg-red-500 text-red-500">Invisible</div>
<div className="bg-gray-100 text-gray-200">Too low contrast</div>
<div className="bg-white text-gray-50">Barely visible</div>
<div className="text-gray-900">Text without background context</div> // Depends on parent

// ✅ ALWAYS DO THIS
<div className="bg-red-100 text-red-900">High contrast</div>
<div className="bg-gray-100 text-gray-900">Clear visibility</div>
<div className="bg-white text-gray-900">Perfect readability</div>
<div className="bg-blue-600 text-white">Excellent contrast</div>
```

## Implementation Checklist

When creating new UI components:

- [ ] Check that text color contrasts with background
- [ ] Test with different viewport sizes
- [ ] Verify hover/focus states have sufficient contrast
- [ ] Ensure disabled states are distinguishable but still readable
- [ ] Test with browser zoom at 200%
- [ ] Validate with accessibility tools (Chrome DevTools, axe DevTools)
- [ ] Consider dark mode if applicable

## AI Assistant Responsibilities

When generating or reviewing code:

1. **Always validate** color combinations for sufficient contrast
2. **Suggest corrections** when low contrast is detected
3. **Use established patterns** from this project (see above examples)
4. **Alert the user** if a color combination might be problematic
5. **Provide alternatives** with better contrast ratios

